# Lets ROM Hub confine plugin subprocesses with a seccomp filter. Without it
# the Hub refuses to run plugins at all unless ROMarr opts out of confinement
# entirely, which is what it used to do -- so this is the difference between
# plugins having a network boundary and having none.
#
# Linux-only, and optional by design: an install without it still runs, logs a
# warning, and says so on the status page.
